		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Minuscule three-tailed newt that lodges in the throat of a sleeping creature and feeds off their food and drink like a parasitic throat tapeworm.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 10, <strong>HP</strong> 1, <strong>ATK</strong> none, <strong>MV</strong> close, <strong>S</strong> -4, <strong>D</strong> +0, <strong>C</strong> +0, <strong>I</strong> +2, <strong>W</strong> +0, <strong>Ch</strong> +0, <strong>AL</strong> <strong>C</strong>, <strong>LV</strong> 0</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Implant</strong>. Implants in the throat of a helpless creature and consumes their food and drink. Target suffers from thirst and starvation.</p><p></p><p><strong>Salt Vulnerability</strong>. 1d6 damage if exposed to raw salt. Eating a mouthful of salt or drinking a pint of saltwater causes alpluachra to detach and be vomited out.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
